WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.170
Moab, Utah, lies near the
centre of the Colorado Plateau:

2
00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:09.530
a high, dry land of canyons,
mesas and sandy plains.

3
00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:12.730
Visitors come for the scenery,
and for off-road driving,

4
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:14.770
mountain biking and hiking.

5
00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:20.710
On the plateau, the surface cover of
scraped test plots took 14 to 34 years to

6
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:21.730
recover.

7
00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:28.790
Across drylands, reported recovery times
range from 2 to more than 3,800 years.

8
00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:33.150
So how can a few tyre tracks
reshape a whole landscape?

9
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.750
In this mission, you'll
compare what tyres,

10
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:39.430
boots and hooves do to
fragile desert ground.

11
00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:43.310
Then you'll weigh how to manage a landscape
that brings in income from visitors

12
00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:45.070
and grazing.

13
00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:50.600
Your mission: explain how off-road driving
can reshape a whole dryland landscape.
